title: 'Transfer on-demand coretime revenue to the broker pallet locally'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-on-demand-para` now books the revenue from the on-demand coretime orders it
    sells, and hands it over to `pallet-broker`, replicating what the Relay Chain's
    on-demand pallet does for the Coretime chain today.

    The spot price paid for an order is kept in the pallet's pot and booked against
    the Relay Chain block the order was placed at, so that the claimer can attribute
    it to the right timeslice. The number of Relay Chain blocks tracked separately is
    bounded by the new `MaxRevenueHistory` config item; once the history is full, new
    revenue is merged into the most recent bucket rather than dropped.

    `pallet-broker` claims that revenue once per timeslice through the new
    `OnDemandRevenue` trait in `fp-coretime`, which `pallet-on-demand-para` implements,
    and which its new `OnDemandRevenue` config item names. Since both pallets live on
    the same chain there is no need for XCM: the funds are transferred straight into
    the broker pot, and the revenue is distributed among the contributors to the
    Instantaneous Coretime Pool within the same block. This replaces the round-trip in
    which the Relay Chain teleports the revenue to the Coretime chain and reports it
    with `notify_revenue`, so the payouts are ready one block earlier than they used
    to be.

    The market is assumed to always be local, so `pallet-broker` no longer calls
    `CoretimeInterface::request_revenue_info_at`. The `notify_revenue` extrinsic and
    the `RevenueInbox` storage item it fills are left in place for now and are removed
    in a follow-up.

    `pallet-on-demand` is also wired into the coretime-westend runtime.
crates:
- name: fp-coretime
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-broker
  bump: major
- name: pallet-on-demand-para
  bump: major
- name: coretime-westend-runtime
  bump: major
